31 files and 3,314 lines in the repository; v1.0 runs 17 of them,
1,887 lines. Where the running system's lines went:

  answering the question      1124   60%  ########################
  the platform around it       486   26%  ##########
  knowing whether it works     277   15%  ######

The part that answers the question is 60% of what runs. The other 40% is
tracing, caching, guarding, shedding load and the suite that says whether the
answers are right. 334 more lines of platform — the gateway and the replay
tools — are not in that count, because v1.0 never imports them; and the retry and
the breaker sit unused inside a file that is. Chapter 31's review found both.

Read it in this order: config, then tools, then agent, then clarity. Four
files and you have the system; the rest is what it took to trust it.
